 connection refusal, DNS/localhost, and the unchanged `.StreamSocket` wrapper.
 
+## Node command-line build (`wasm/build-node.sh`)
+
+`wasm/build-node.sh [BUILD_DIR]` relinks the runtime (no recompilation) into
+`BUILD_DIR/bin-node` as a Node-only command-line ooRexx (`-sNODERAWFS=1
+-sENVIRONMENT=node`, `wasm/node-pre.js`): it sees the host file system and
+the host environment variables, and ADDRESS commands run as host processes
+(`child_process.spawnSync` on the interpreter thread, so concurrent Rexx
+threads can run commands; ADDRESS ... WITH redirection is supported).
+`bin-node/rexx` and `bin-node/rexxc` are launchers; `rexxc` is a multi-call
+entry of the same `rexx.js` (`wasm/rexxc-main.cpp`).  Error numbers seen by
+Rexx programs (RC of CD, stream `ERROR:n`, SysMkDir, ...) are the Linux ones,
+not the WASI ones of the Emscripten libc (`HOST_ERRNO`).
+
+    ./wasm/build-node.sh /tmp/oorexx-wasm-build
+    ./wasm/tests/qualify-node-cli.sh /tmp/oorexx-wasm-build/bin-node
+
 ## Browser status
 
 The generated `rexx.js/rexx.wasm/rexx.data` target `node,web,worker`. A pthread
@@ -108,7 +125,7 @@ browser; see the limits below).
 * UDP/datagram semantics are not qualified.
